            <description><![CDATA[<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } .when, .earlier { color: #9a9a9a; } hr { border-color: #444; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
h3 { font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 4px; }
.when { font-weight: 400; color: #777; }
.earlier { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #777; margin: 18px 0 2px; }
hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; margin: 16px 0 0; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1512) <span class="when">Oct 13, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Kitsu's comments come into a review made from Kitsu.</b> Each clip carries what was said on its task in Kitsu, with the replies, as notes: the author, the date, the version it was about and the status it set. A comment on an older version sits on the newest loaded one, marked with its own version. Refreshing the list brings new comments and replies. They are not sent back to Kitsu on a publish. Show or hide them from the Kitsu window, or Review ▸ Notes ▸ Show Kitsu Comments.</li>
<li><b>Joining a review tells you where it stands.</b> An empty window shows "Joining the review…", then "Connected. Looking for the host…". A review that has <b>ended</b> says so at once; a review nobody is hosting says so after a few seconds, and names who else is waiting. There is a Leave Review button, and the same words appear over the picture when the window already has media.</li>
<li>Clicking a panel while another app is in front brings all of Asobi forward, not the one panel. Panels sit behind other apps more reliably when Asobi is not the app in front.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1476) <span class="when">Oct 12, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>DPX sequences play.</b> 8, 10, 12 and 16-bit DPX files open and play like any other image sequence, read as the color space set for DPX in Settings, Color.</li>
<li>A tall floating Playlist with thumbnails could stop the app. Fixed.</li>
<li>Small fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1441) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Network is in the Review menu.</b> Review ▸ Network; it was under Window. It is also in the right-click Review menu.</li>
<li><b>A playlist on a network drive no longer slows the window.</b> Whether each clip's file is there is checked in the background.</li>
<li><b>Locate Media… reads a folder in the background.</b> A line above the toolbar says how far it has got.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1430) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Small fixes.</li>
</ul>
